BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:After Death Planning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T120000
UID:69fe5ffdc7d3cd580057fced@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you considered what will happen with the physical part of
  yourself once you have concluded this human experience? Gone are the days
  with only two options of cremation or burial. What is a natural burial\, 
 water cremation\, or body composting? What if we don’t have the money to
  secure any of these? Let’s learn from each other as we explore what it 
 looks like in today’s landscape of after death planning. Presented by Sa
 rah Vevoda\, LMSW\, elder care consultant and end of life doula.
LOCATION:Beaverton City Library\, Meeting Room A
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe5ffdc7d3cd580057fced
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
