BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Important Documents for the Elder Years
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260611T120000
UID:69fe2891f56bd86e00ae6696@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What is the difference between a power of attorney\, advance d
 irective\, will\, trust\, guardian\, and conservator? What other important
  documents might come into play if we become sick\, injured\, or are simpl
 y in our later years? This discussion aims to bring clarity to the often c
 onfusing roadmap of necessary end of life documents while clarifying impor
 tant details that many times are overlooked. Presented by Sarah Vevoda\, L
 MSW\, elder care consultant and end of life doula.
LOCATION:Beaverton City Library\, Meeting Room A
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe2891f56bd86e00ae6696
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
