BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Storytime
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T120000
UID:69af4f5db0595799c0a1fe5c@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Storytime Wednesdays at 11:00 a.m.\nTime for stories\, bubbles
 \, and songs! Following storytime Mrs. Emily will teach children to identi
 fy and sound out letters of the alphabet and counting basics. Parents and 
 caregivers learn meaningful techniques that will help expand learning expe
 riences at home with your child. Drop in\, no registration required.\nIf a
 ccommodations would help you attend one of our library events or classes\,
  please ask. Our library events are always free!
LOCATION:North Plains Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69af4f5db0595799c0a1fe5c
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Getting Started with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260608T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260608T183000
UID:69fe27f0f6bd012f00669c39@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about artificial intelligence but not sure where to be
 gin? In this session\, we’ll explore the basics of AI tools like ChatGPT
  and how they can support your everyday work\, learning\, and creativity. 
 We’ll focus on using AI as a partner rather than a replacement—so you 
 stay in control while getting the benefits of faster ideas\, clearer writi
 ng\, and smarter organization. Presenter Bio: Crystal Trice has over 20 ye
 ars of experience in libraries and education and is the founder of Scissor
 s & Glue\, LLC. She leads interactive trainings and workshops on topics ra
 nging from project management to artificial intelligence\, helping librari
 es and schools spark positive change. Based near Portland\, Oregon\, Cryst
 al enjoys life with her husband\, a small menagerie of farm animals\, and 
 an endless supply of sticky notes and colorful pens.
LOCATION:Beaverton City Library\, Meeting Rooms A & B
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe27f0f6bd012f00669c39
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Teen Time: Writing Workshop with Jamie Pacton
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T150000
UID:699e68f11e64afd01e5de1ef@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join local bestselling\, award-winning author Jamie Pacton for
  a lively talk on writing and publishing novels across genres and age grou
 ps. Learn how to move from idea to outline\, draft to finished book\, and 
 on to publication. Come learn\, create\, and connect with the writing comm
 unity.\nRegistration preferred\; walk-ins welcome.
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Shute Park
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699e68f11e64afd01e5de1ef
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Reading Kick-off & WCCLS Birthday with Aztec Dance Huitzilo
 pochtli
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T140000
UID:6a02243c703c33630026e0b9@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading Kick-off & WCCLS Birthday with\nAztec Dance Hui
 tzilopochtli Saturday\, June 13\nth\nat 1:00 p.m. at Jessie Mays Community
  Center\nHappy 50th birthday\, Washington County Cooperative Library Servi
 ces (WCCLS) Experience the Rhythm of History!  Join us for an afternoon of
  traditional Aztec dance. Immerse yourself in the vibrant colors\, powerfu
 l storytelling\, and rich cultural heritage of this incredible troupe. The
  performance will take place\, followed by celebratory birthday treats\, a
 vailable while supplies last. Fun for all ages! Drop in\, no registration 
 required.\nYou’re Invited! WCCLS is Turning 50\nOur friends at Washingto
 n County Cooperative Library Services (WCCLS) are celebrating their 50th b
 irthday! Starting June 1\, visit us in person to:\n• Get a special editi
 on library card while supplies last.\n• Pick up a passport and collect s
 tamps from the 16 WCCLS libraries. Starting July 1\, show your completed p
 assport to library staff and take home a Wallace puzzle while supplies las
 t (1 per household).
LOCATION:North Plains Public Library\, Jessie Mays Community Center 30975 
 NW Hillcrest St\, North Plains\, OR 97133
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a02243c703c33630026e0b9
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drop-in Tech Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260630T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260630T120000
UID:688a54b9639e1e9694a3d69a@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Whether you're a beginner trying to navigate your first smartp
 hone or a more experienced user looking to troubleshoot an issue with your
  computer or assemble a custom PC build\, we’re here to help. Drop-in to
  ask questions and receive one-on-one assistance with a variety of topics\
 , including but not limited to:\nBasic computer skills (e.g. how to use a 
 mouse\, open and close programs\, create and save documents)\nSetting up a
 nd using an email account\nUsing search engines and the internet\nTransfer
 ring files and photos between devices\nBasic smartphone and tablet skills 
 (e.g. how to make a call\, send a text message\, install and use an app)\n
 No matter your level of experience\, we welcome you to join us! No registr
 ation required. Please bring your device with you if you have one\, as thi
 s will allow us to better assist you with any specific issues you may be e
 xperiencing.
LOCATION:Aloha Community Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/688a54b9639e1e9694a3d69a
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
