BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Leathercraft | Artesanía en Cuero
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T170000
UID:69e2e96adefec6489cbe9370@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn the creative and practical skill of leather working! We
 'll teach you the basics of how to cut\, sew\, and carve intricate design
 s into leather. Practice by making key chains\, cup sleeves\, and skillet 
 holders you can take home and use afterwards. Let's see what you come up 
 with!\nThis program is for adults.\n¡Aprende la técnica creativa y prác
 tica del trabajo con cuero! Te enseñaremos los fundamentos para cortar\, 
 coser y tallar diseños intrincados en cuero. Practica creando llaveros\, 
 fundas para tazas y soportes para sartenes que podrás llevarte a casa y u
 sar después. ¡A ver qué creas!\nEste programa es para adultos.
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e2e96adefec6489cbe9370
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Teen Crafternoon: Make Your Own Book [at Bethany Library Annex]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260624T160000
UID:69f676edb1e102b0f3d94c78@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Participants will learn how to create their own book! In this 
 afternoon workshop\, Sara White\, proprietor of\nAlluvium Press & Bindery\
 nin Portland will teach teens to sew two simple and useful blank book stru
 ctures: the 3- and 5-hole pamphlet stitch. We will talk a bit about the hi
 story of sewn pamphlets and material qualities to consider when binding bo
 oks. We will look at artistic and literary examples that incorporate the p
 amphlet structure\, and as time allows\, we'll decorate our own books usin
 g a stenciling technique called pochoir printing. No experience is necessa
 ry\, however this activity will require detailed and intricate work\, part
 icipants will be using needles and Xacto knives. Latex gloves and thimbles
  will be provided if you want to use them\, but feel free to bring protect
 ive wear from home if needed. Registration Required for ages 11-18 only.
LOCATION:Bethany Library\, Bethany Annex
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f676edb1e102b0f3d94c78
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
