SUMMARY:Medieval Dance Class | Clase de Danza Medieval
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260702T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260702T210000
UID:69cec9f8213814b1b522ca59@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:If you're fascinated by history and love to dance\, join us fo
 r a Medieval Dance Class! Learn authentic dances from the time period and 
 immerse yourself in the rhythm and culture of yesteryear. No experience ne
 cessary—just bring your enthusiasm and get ready to have fun! This progr
 am is for teens and adults.\nSi te fascina la historia y te encanta bailar
 \, ¡ven a nuestra clase de danza medieval! Aprende bailes auténticos de 
 la época y sumérgete en el ritmo y la cultura de antaño. No se necesita
  experiencia\, ¡solo traiga su entusiasmo y prepárese para divertirse! E
 ste programa es para adolescentes y adultos.
LOCATION:Cornelius Public Library
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cec9f8213814b1b522ca59
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Atelier: Charcoal Drawing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260603T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260603T193000
UID:69f2686766c3387a9d0851f0@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Bring a friend and join us Wednesday nights for an art worksho
 p! Enjoy dedicated time for art and unwinding. In the month of June we wil
 l host two classes exploring drawing with charcoal. We will use a differen
 t beginner-friendly still life in each class. During the sessions we will 
 draft simplified shapes and use charcoal to block in values\, with a focus
  on constructive corrections\, adding highlights and detail. All materials
  are provided and all skill levels are welcome.\nFor adults and teens 14+.
  Registration is required. Held in the Makerspace.
LOCATION:Tualatin Public Library\, Makerspace
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f2686766c3387a9d0851f0
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Inclusive Pathways to Kindergarten
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260603T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260603T193000
UID:699f4f5b1c129a205bcd20eb@wccls.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The purpose of these 5 series is to help families with childre
 n who may need additional support\, including those with disabilities\, to
  learn tools and strategies to support their successful transition to kind
 ergarten in fall\, 2026. Children and their caregivers will engage in acti
 vities that target academic and social-emotional learning using evidence-b
 ased practices such as predictable routines\, visual support and simple as
 sistive technology. Families will learn how to develop meaningful partners
 hips with their schools to ensure the best start for their learner.\nRegis
 tration required.
LOCATION:Hillsboro Public Library\, Shute Park
URL:https://wccls.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f4f5b1c129a205bcd20eb
X-SOURCE:WCCLS Libraries
END:VEVENT
